1
00:00:00,720 --> 00:00:09,099
Welcome to Athena, a Web3 Smart Contract Security Audit Agent powered by GLM 5.1 Long Horizon Task Capabilities.

2
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:10,560
Let's see how it works.

3
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:14,320
Step 1. Loading the audit skill.

4
00:00:14,740 --> 00:00:18,300
Athena uses 12 specialized agents running in parallel,

5
00:00:18,679 --> 00:00:21,420
each focusing on a different vulnerability class,

6
00:00:21,899 --> 00:00:27,980
including access control, reentrancy, flash loans, and oracle manipulation.

7
00:00:29,059 --> 00:00:33,939
Step 2. Selecting the audit target, VulnerableBank,

8
00:00:34,299 --> 00:00:36,579
a classic reentrancy test case.

9
00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:41,780
Notice the bug. External call happens before the state update.

10
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:46,679
Step 3. Spawning three sub-agents in parallel.

11
00:00:47,479 --> 00:00:51,899
Static analysis, proof-of-concept generation, and fuzz testing,

12
00:00:52,359 --> 00:00:53,799
all running simultaneously.

13
00:00:55,039 --> 00:01:00,359
Step 4. Sub-agent 1 completes dual-engine static analysis.

14
00:01:00,880 --> 00:01:04,540
Slither found three issues, Aderyn found four.

15
00:01:04,959 --> 00:01:08,500
After deduplication, we have four unique findings,

16
00:01:08,980 --> 00:01:12,519
including two high-severity reentrancy vulnerabilities.

17
00:01:13,719 --> 00:01:19,340
Step 5. Sub-agent 2 generates a proof-of-concept attack contract.

18
00:01:19,340 --> 00:01:24,379
The attacker deposits 1 ETH, then exploits the reentrancy bug

19
00:01:24,379 --> 00:01:26,879
to drain the entire bank balance.

20
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:32,239
Step 6. Sub-agent 3 runs fuzz testing with Foundry.

21
00:01:32,439 --> 00:01:36,280
768 fuzz runs, all six tests pass.

22
00:01:36,819 --> 00:01:39,640
The bank balance drops from 10 ETH to zero,

23
00:01:40,079 --> 00:01:42,480
confirming the vulnerability is exploitable.

24
00:01:43,739 --> 00:01:46,079
Step 7. Consolidating results.

25
00:01:47,079 --> 00:01:49,359
Static analysis found four issues.

26
00:01:49,680 --> 00:01:51,519
POC confirmed the attack.

27
00:01:51,859 --> 00:01:55,299
Fuzz testing verified it 768 times.

28
00:01:55,620 --> 00:01:56,519
Overall rating?

29
00:01:57,159 --> 00:01:58,819
S. Critical severity.

30
00:01:59,519 --> 00:02:00,439
Recommended fix?

31
00:02:01,060 --> 00:02:03,299
Use the checks-effects-interactions pattern.

32
00:02:04,120 --> 00:02:07,859
Step 8. On-chain certification.

33
00:02:08,840 --> 00:02:13,000
The audit result is attested on Ethereum Sepolia using EAS,

34
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:18,340
then an Athena Warrior NFT is minted as a verifiable certificate

35
00:02:18,340 --> 00:02:23,680
with 262,144 possible trait combinations.
